<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Old Quarter</span>
<h1>Old Quarter by Motorbike: Motorbike Day-Ride Ideas in Hanoi</h1>
<p>A day ride is the shape freedom takes in Hanoi. From the rental counter in Long Bien, the day opens in every direction: the river and its bridges, the lanes of the Old Quarter, the lake edges that cool the city, the wider districts beyond. The ideas on this page are deliberately flexible, because a day built rigidly around opening hours, traffic wishes and weather hopes is a day that breaks. A day built from loose blocks holds together whatever the city decides.</p>
<p>This guide belongs to the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">motorbike rental in the Hanoi Old Quarter</a> hub, draws on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource for machines and prices, and pairs with the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding skills and wider trips. The honest framing: no invented journey times, no live-traffic promises, no made-up parking rules, and every ride starts from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">How to read a day-ride idea</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The Hoan Kiem loop</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">River and bridge riding</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">Lakes and greener edges</a></li>
